        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Using polymeric sand well comes down to controlling water. Start with dry pavers, dry joints and a dry forecast. Fill the joints to the right depth and level, compact and refill until they stay full, then clean every grain off the surface before misting in light, patient passes.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If something goes wrong, fix it properly rather than patching over it: remove failed sand fully and reinstall. And if you have not chosen a product yet, match it to your joint width first. Our <a href="/best-polymeric-sand/">best polymeric sand</a> guide sorts the options by exactly that.
          </p>
